Nexus 0.13.4 client cancellation after uncertain execution transport failure.
Upstream: d60ff582fde90c59726336c0dbdf3e8286e9df7a.
Reason: retain at most 64 exact handle-owned IDs, reject new execution at capacity,
and use the existing independent control connection without replay. Values track
whether cancellation received a true ACK. Backend locking is not FIFO: success
clears only already ACKed predecessors. A later false after a true ACK removes the
exact ID; unacknowledged false remains retryable because POST registration may
still be pending. Health/error responses never clear IDs. Close clears all.
Probe: scripts/nexus/probe_cancel_after_disconnect.py; tests/nexus_bridge/.
Removal: only after a pinned upstream fix passes the probe, N0 and N3 gates.
N9 packaging must carry this patch until that revalidation.

